message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Recurrent Summary Memory: bounded-state in-context reinforcement learning"
type: software
version: 0.8.0
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous authors"
abstract: >-
  Code, configurations, pre-declarations and summary results for Recurrent
  Summary Memory (RSM), a Transformer policy for in-context reinforcement
  learning that combines exact attention over a short working buffer with a
  fixed-capacity summary rewritten at every segment boundary, trained with
  AMAGO's off-policy actor-critic and compared with full-history, accumulating
  (Memo), recurrent (GRU) and sliding-window memories on Dark Key-to-Door,
  CountRecallMedium, a passive T-Maze and MazeRunner.
